From: MeowArchMobile
Subject: [PATCH] client/usb_windows.cpp: a failed power-notification window must
 not abort the server

usb_init() starts two detached threads. One polls for USB devices; the other,
_power_notification_thread(), builds a hidden message-only window so the server
can react to WM_POWERBROADCAST / PBT_APMRESUMEAUTOMATIC by kicking USB devices
after a resume. Both RegisterClassExW and CreateWindowExW were checked with
LOG(FATAL), which aborts the whole daemon.

That makes a cosmetic optimization load-bearing for the server's life. The
thread's own comment already anticipated the case -- "If adb runs from a
non-interactive service account, this might not work (not sure)" -- and the
answer to the unsure was to abort.

CreateWindowExW fails whenever the process has no desktop to create a window
on, which is normal for a detached adb server: session 0 isolation, a Windows
service account, a session whose desktop is not yet created, or a machine with
no interactive session at all. The process then dies before it writes the
"OK\n" ack that launch_server() waits for, so the client that spawned it
reports only

    could not read ok from ADB Server
    * failed to start daemon
    error: cannot connect to daemon

with no mention of windows, desktops or power notifications, and every
subsequent adb command fails the same way. Measured under wine 11.21 in a
container with no display, foreground, which names the actual site:

    00f0:err:winediag:nodrv_CreateWindow Application tried to create a window,
        but no driver could be loaded.
    F adb.exe : usb_windows.cpp:234 CreateWindowExW failed: Success. (0)

(GetLastError() is 0 because the failure comes from wine's display-less path,
not from a Win32 error code being set -- which is exactly why the fatal message
is useless as a diagnosis.) Under Xvfb the same binary starts normally, which
pins the cause to the window, not to the sockets.

Downgrade both to LOG(WARNING) and return from the thread. What is lost is the
resume kick: a device that was mid-handshake when the machine slept may need
re-plugging. The device_poll_thread() beside it keeps running and keeps finding
devices, and everything else is unaffected. Killing the server over it is a much
worse outcome than the degraded case it prevents -- and on a headless host there
is no interactive session to resume in the first place.

This is the third Windows-only defect the cross build has exposed (after the
wstat struct mismatch in 0004 and the root-dir walk in 0005), and like the other
two it is invisible on POSIX, where usb_init() comes from usb_linux.cpp and
creates no window.

--- a/client/usb_windows.cpp
+++ b/client/usb_windows.cpp
diff --git a/client/usb_windows.cpp b/client/usb_windows.cpp
index b17c480..a607e7b 100644
--- a/client/usb_windows.cpp
+++ b/client/usb_windows.cpp
@@ -223,16 +223,42 @@ static void _power_notification_thread() {
     wndclass.lpfnWndProc = _power_window_proc;
     wndclass.hInstance = instance;
     wndclass.lpszClassName = kPowerNotificationWindowClassName;
+    // This thread exists only to receive WM_POWERBROADCAST so that USB devices
+    // get kicked after a resume. That is an optimization, not a requirement:
+    // without it, a device that was mid-handshake when the machine slept may
+    // need to be re-plugged, while everything else works normally. So a failure
+    // to build the window is a warning and this thread gives up, rather than a
+    // fatal error that takes the whole server down.
+    //
+    // The upstream LOG(FATAL) is not hypothetical. CreateWindowExW fails
+    // whenever the process has no window station/desktop to create a window on,
+    // which is the case for an adb server running detached from any interactive
+    // session (a Windows service, session 0, a session whose desktop is not
+    // yet created) and for adb.exe under a headless wine. The comment above
+    // this function already anticipated it -- "If adb runs from a
+    // non-interactive service account, this might not work (not sure)" -- and
+    // then made the unsure case abort the daemon: the client that spawned the
+    // server sees only "could not read ok from ADB Server" / "failed to start
+    // daemon", because the process died before writing its ack. Measured under
+    // wine 11.21 in a container with no X display: the foreground server
+    // aborted with exactly
+    //     usb_windows.cpp:234 CreateWindowExW failed: Success. (0)
+    // and every client command failed with cannot connect to daemon; the same
+    // binary under Xvfb started normally. (GetLastError() is 0 because the
+    // failure comes from wine's display-less nodrv_CreateWindow path, not from
+    // a Win32 error being set.)
     if (!RegisterClassExW(&wndclass)) {
-        LOG(FATAL) << "RegisterClassExW failed: "
-                   << android::base::SystemErrorCodeToString(GetLastError());
+        LOG(WARNING) << "RegisterClassExW failed, power notifications disabled: "
+                     << android::base::SystemErrorCodeToString(GetLastError());
+        return;
     }
 
     if (!CreateWindowExW(WS_EX_NOACTIVATE, kPowerNotificationWindowClassName,
                          L"ADB Power Notification Window", WS_POPUP, 0, 0, 0, 0, nullptr, nullptr,
                          instance, nullptr)) {
-        LOG(FATAL) << "CreateWindowExW failed: "
-                   << android::base::SystemErrorCodeToString(GetLastError());
+        LOG(WARNING) << "CreateWindowExW failed, power notifications disabled: "
+                     << android::base::SystemErrorCodeToString(GetLastError());
+        return;
     }
 
     MSG msg;
